DAY 01 | C# Introduction

What is C#?

C# (pronounced "C-Sharp") is a popular programming language created by Microsoft that is used to give instructions to computers. Think of it as a tool for writing the digital recipes that make software work.
Here is the easiest way to understand it:
What is it used for?
• Video Games: It is the main language used to build games in the Unity engine (like Among Us or Hollow Knight).
• Websites: It powers the invisible "back-end" of major websites, handling data and security.
• Apps: It is used to make apps for Windows computers, iPhones, and Android phones.

In this practice, I learned the basic structure of a C# console application.

